<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pellestrina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pellestrina is a long, narrow barrier island between the Venetian lagoon and the Adriatic Sea, south of the Lido and north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chioggia">Chioggia</a>. Its fishing villages were among the old lagoon settlements, and in 810 it was overrun by the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-italy">Pepin of Italy</a>. In the 18th century the republic protected it from the sea with the great stone sea walls known as the Murazzi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pellestrina.jpg" alt="Pellestrina" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gugganij · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venice_Lagoon_Pellestrina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
